q
1 0 0 1 57.02362 657.8701 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 71.5 Tm /F1 9 Tf 11.5 TL (When we turn 96 numbers into just 10 numbers we lose most of the details about the shape and the timing of the) Tj T* (heartbeat. Stuff like min, max, median, skewness and kurtosis dont care about the order of the values at all so if you mix) Tj T* (up all the points the numbers stay the same but the heartbeat would look totally different. So we lose things like where) Tj T* (the signal goes down and for how long, how wide the big spike is, what the wave after it looks like and how far apart the) Tj T* (waves are. I kept argmax and argmin to keep a little bit of timing but thats only 2 points out of 96. Also the dataset was) Tj T* (already z normalised so mean, std, RMS and energy were the same for every signal and we had to throw them out) Tj T* (because they tell the model nothing.) Tj T* ET
